.\n4.2 Most important symptoms and effects, both acute and delayed\nHints for Physician: Symptoms\nSee Section 11 for additonal information on health hazards\n4.3 Indication of any immediate medical attention and special treatment needed\nFirst Aid: Inhalation\nRemove casualty to fresh air and keep warm and at rest. If breathing is irregular or stopped, administer \nartificial respiration. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBiosynth (https://www.genoprice.com/biosynth.htm)\nciteturn48search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6.7 years ago; M-3595 [3370-81-8] 98,5 3-O-Methyl-D-glucopyranoside 2,5 61 €\nB-1520 [57765-22-7] 98 6-Benzyloxygramine 1 49 €\nN-4350 [3767-28-0] 99 4-Nitrophenyl-alpha-D-glucopyranoside 2,5 44 €\nC-3930 [122509-72-2] 99 6-Chloro-5-fluoroindole 0,1 41 €\nA-8240 [87-72-9] 99 L-Arabinose 100 55 €\nN-2260 [33993-25-8] 99 2-Naphthyl-beta-D-galactopyranoside 0,25 37 €\nC-4600 [4792-67-0] 98 5-Chloroindole-2-carboxylic acid ethyl ester 5 51 €\nH-8140 [153-98-0] 99 5-Hydroxytryptamine hydrochloride 2,5 46 €\nF-4540 [399-51-9] 99 6-Fluoroindole 2,5 38 €\nH-6200 [54-16-0] 98 5-Hydroxyindole-3-acetic acid 0,5 41 €\nB-8000 [4263-52-9]   2-Bromoethanesulfonic acid, sodium salt 250 40 €\nN-4030 [10139-02-3]   4-Nitrophenyl-N-acetyl-alpha-D-glucosaminide 0,25 44 €\nM-5738 [67909-30-2] 99 4-Methylumbelliferyl-beta-D-mannopyranoside 0,05 51 €\nF-6670 [191927-74-9] 98 7-Fluorotryptamine, free base 0,05 51 €\nC-7003 [50909-86-9]   Coelenterazine h 0,001 67 €\nT-8100 [61-54-1] 98 Tryptamine, free base 25 44 €\nH-8500 [154-02-9] 99 5-Hydroxytryptophol 0,1 37 €\nB-8440 [52415-29-9] 98 6-Bromoindole 2,5 41 €\nI-6200 [107475-12-7] 99 Y™-phos · 2 AMPD 0,1 49 €\nC-3928 [169674-57-1]   5-Chloro-6-fluoroindole 0,025 55 €\nL-8600 [521-31-3] 95 Luminol 25 57 €\nM-5024 [951-55-3] 98 5-Methyl-DL-tryptophan 0,25 44 €\nH-2250 [56-92-8]   Histamine dihydrochloride Ph. Eur IV 10 36 €\nN-4150 [1226-39-7] 99 4-Nitrophenyl-beta-D-fucopyranosi